#!/usr/bin/env python3
# tt version 13
"""Timing wrapper and its reports.

    tt <target> -- <command> [args...]
    tt harvest [--json]
    tt report [--since WHEN] [--until WHEN] [--project PREFIX] [--all] [--json]
    tt latency check    [--project PREFIX] [--json]
    tt latency escalate [--project PREFIX] [--dry-run] [--json]
    tt latency verify   TASK --after TIMESTAMP [--dry-run] [--json]

The wrapper runs the command with stdin, stdout, and stderr passed through, and appends
one JSON line describing the run to the log. `harvest` moves checkouts' fallback logs
into the shared log; `report` harvests, then summarises test timings per project;
`latency` judges the log against latency.toml beside this script's parent and files
stop-work incidents in tasks. Projects carry a byte-identical copy at tools/tt.
Vendored from https://github.com/khughitt/ops (bin/tt); never edit the copy, see tools/README.md.
Standard library only. Reference: ops docs/tooling.md, docs/test-execution-policy.md.
"""
